<title>SPAIN: Peseta debt/interbank closing report.</title>
<headline>Peseta debt/interbank closing report.</headline>
<dateline>MADRID 1996-09-27</dateline>
<text>
<p>Spanish government bonds were off highs in late trade on Friday, although the bono-bund spread stayed down at 178 basis points versus 190 at Thursday's close.</p>
<p>Dealers said the 1997 budget, details of which were announced this afternoon, provided few surprises for the market, which had already rallied on expected stringent measures.</p>
<p>One economist said even though a forecast rise of 1.7 percent in 1997 government expenditure was more restrictive than most were expecting, the bond market seemed more concerned by the prospects for a cut in the Bank of Spain's key money rate next week.</p>
</text>
